#[Overall Rules]
#Three-part syntax: lines beginning with # are explanatory content (rules, dictionaries, and section titles) that tools do not extract but models must read | ===description/absolute/path/=== opens a directory section | every other non-empty line in a directory section is an Entry
#Directory example: ===Backend Index{{.RepoRootSlash}}=== is “description + absolute directory path + ===” on one line and opens one directory section
#Entry format: filename[tag]: F:function | R:relationships | A:interface | S:information; exactly one line; all four fields present; use - for an empty field
#F scope: write one short, precise core-function anchor; semantic completeness takes priority when a few more words are needed; do not translate filenames, pile up several responsibilities, or use mass-produced sentence patterns
#R scope: list only strong cross-file dependencies as comma-separated exact paths or module names; omit logging, generic utilities, and framework-provided dependencies; never mechanically copy import or dependency lists
#A scope: list only APIs, entry points, or contracts exposed by this file; omit internal functions; use - when none exists
#S discipline: write only information that cannot be inferred from filename + tag + F + R + A but that the model must know to understand the system or modify code; both tests must pass; prohibit evolution narratives and time-dependent information such as versions, dates, or repair history; quotas are declared below
#Multiple tag systems: a large project may define an independent rule block for each technical domain, such as backend, frontend, or database, with separate A/B/D values; the same letter may mean different things across systems, but each block must define it clearly
